# Template for the real manifest.
#
# Copy to ~/.dotfiles-local/backup.manifest (NOT into the repo) and edit.
# One path per line. `#` starts a comment. Supported prefixes: ~, $HOME,
# $DOTFILES_SECRETS_DIR, and $DOTFILES_LOCAL_DIR (also ${…} forms).
# Every entry must resolve to an absolute path. Relative paths and other
# variable/command expansion are rejected before vault mutation. Sources that
# overlap the selected portable-artifact destination are also rejected;
# missing absolute paths are warned/skipped.
#
# Recommended (single canonical tree — see README § Secrets layout):
# This row publishes as <snapshot>/payload/secrets/ so a replacement Mac may
# use a different short username without changing the restore command.
#
~/.secrets
#
# ~/.secrets/ layout (all vault-backed, never in git):
#
#   ~/.secrets/
#   ├── env.sh                          # sourced only by interactive zsh
#   ├── ssh/                            # → ~/.ssh/* via symlinks.tsv
#   ├── config/
#   │   ├── gh/hosts.yml                # → ~/.config/gh/hosts.yml
#   │   └── env/                        # → ~/.config/env/ (per-tool env files)
#   └── apps/
#       ├── canary-mail/                # realms + plist — make backup-canary / restore-canary
#       ├── shottr/                     # cc.ffitch.shottr.plist — make backup-shottr / restore-shottr
#       ├── dato/                       # full primary prefs — make backup-dato / restore-dato
#       ├── deskflow/                   # Mac configuration + TLS archive — make backup-deskflow
#       ├── thaw/                       # manual profile export/import
#       ├── raycast/                    # manual .rayconfig / export bundles
#       ├── vscode/                     # token-bearing MCP/profile data — manual restore
#       ├── sublime-text/               # Monokai Pro license settings (not in repo)
#       └── transmit/                   # manual .transmitservers exports
#
# All of the above are covered by the single ~/.secrets manifest line.
#
# Migrating from an old manifest that listed ~/.config/* or ~/.ssh/* paths?
# Move files into the ~/.secrets/ tree above, then `make link`.
